Hi team,

Short summary of Friday's incident in order-service.

What happened: memory grew from 300 MB to 1.8 GB over 6 hours and the
pods were OOM-killed. Logs showed 'MaxListenersExceededWarning: Possible
EventEmitter memory leak detected. 11 message listeners added'.

Root cause: every HTTP request called redisSubscriber.on('message', ...)
and never removed the listener, so listeners and their closures piled up.

Fix: register the listener once at startup, and use emitter.once() or
emitter.off() for per-request listeners. We also added a heap snapshot
alert using 'node --heapsnapshot-near-heap-limit=2'.

The full postmortem is attached.

Thanks,
Priya

